Article 28
(1) The Regent implements policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women to eliminate all forms of discrimination and acts of Violence Against Women.
(2) Regional Apparatus with responsibility for Women implements policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women that have been established and their implementation is carried out in cooperation and coordination with relevant Regional Apparatus, law enforcement, community institutions, universities, and the community.
(3) The implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be in the form of:
a. policy analysis;
b. advocacy;
c. coordination and communication;
d. socialization;
e. education;
f. training;
g. facilitation;
h. provision of services; and
i. other forms.
jdih.pangandarankab.go.id 16

Article 34
(1) Protection services for women are provided in the form of:
a. protection of the victim's personal security from physical and mental threats;
b. health services according to medical needs; c. medical services for the purpose of evidence in the legal field;
d. maintaining the confidentiality of the victim's identity;
e. providing testimony during court hearings without facing the suspect; f. spiritual guidance services; and/or
g. protection for women who work as laborers or workers in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(2) Protection of the victim's personal security from physical and mental threats as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a is carried out by family, law enforcement officials, social institutions, and other parties either temporarily or based on a court-issued Protection order.

Article 18
(1) The implementation of protection for homeless women is in the context of providing protection and prevention against forms of violence caused by the absence of shelter or permanent residence.
(2) Homeless women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall receive the right to protection for:
a. decent housing;
b. health and social security;
c. population administration registration;
d. opportunities to obtain skills to improve economic status; and
e. access to information and legal consultation services.

Article 7
Empowerment of women in the social and cultural field is implemented through;
a. improvement of knowledge, attitudes and skills to encourage the fulfillment of tiered education in accordance with potential to improve social status;
b. improvement of awareness, willingness and ability to overcome health problems through quality promotive, preventive, curative, and rehabilitative efforts primarily in the field of reproductive health;
c. improvement of awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration; and
d. facilitation and efforts to preserve customs and traditions and development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women.

